 17592186045453 13194139535627 true] [17592186358208 1111 #uuid "4064223c-ad38-598c-abdb-84c9c7518a0f" 13194139535627 true] [17592186358209 1034 "9" 13194139535627 true] [17592186358209 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535627 true] [17592186358209 1111 #uuid "36a1677c-6a52-5112-ac7a-da0f9975fff0" 13194139535627 true] [17592186358210 1034 "3" 13194139535627 true] [17592186358210 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535627 true] [17592186358210 1111 #uuid "1d6f2683-aad9-5c97-8ccc-613e305b9d74" 13194139535627 true] [17592186358211 1034 "\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}" 13194139535627 true] [17592186358211 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535627 true] [17592186358211 1111 #uuid "1cf49e73-6903-5817-8ca0-2ca2215bbe52" 13194139535627 true] [17592186358212 1034 "\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}" 13194139535627 true] [17592186358212 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535627 true] [17592186358212 1111 #uuid "aa56137b-0d0d-5428-85a1-5d6a3bc39b54" 13194139535627 true] [17592186358213 1017 #edb/ref 17592186358214 13194139535627 true] [17592186358213 1089 "q-346618" 13194139535627 true] [17592186358213 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535627 true] [17592186358213 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535627 true] [17592186358213 1113 #uuid "e50983a7-5268-5d47-b86f-cc6d21c90477" 13194139535627 true] [17592186358213 1145 "First, we substitute $u={x}^{3}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u={x}^{2}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to -\\infty $ when $x\\to -\\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u={x}^{3}$ is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $-\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $-\\infty $ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{5}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}{5}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{{5}^{u}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}]}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[{5}^{u}]_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(1-{5}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(1-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{5}^{a})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, recall the end behavior of the function $y={5}^{a},$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{5}^{a}=0$\n\n- ${lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{5}^{a}=\\infty $\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067475/assets/c0c7699b036ebd8779cd6c3d3143cdcca6312834ee731e144e38488124164f43.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{x}^{2}\\cdot {5}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(1-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{5}^{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535627 true] [17592186358214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358215 13194139535627 true] [17592186358214 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358216 13194139535627 true] [17592186358214 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535627 true] [17592186358214 1041 "field-1" 13194139535627 true] [17592186358214 1104 #edb/ref 17592186358215 13194139535627 true] [17592186358214 1110 #uuid "c960562e-66f4-5a39-8f69-70987c9f9b6e" 13194139535627 true] [17592186358215 1034 "\\frac{1}{3\\ln(5)}" 13194139535627 true] [17592186358215 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535627 true] [17592186358215 1111 #uuid "f2cdade1-bc33-5b7c-b6b7-8a2436e23303" 1319413953562